Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:48:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: no row of the player information scrolls where it
 can take two lines
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The colour of the film on the video page and the metadata sent on the overview
were rows whose value scrolled when it was wider than its room. Kodi moves such
a label all the time that it is too wide: it is read badly (a picture of the
panel caught the colour as "Γ.709", the end of "BT.709" mid-scroll) and is
drawn again in every frame while it moves, over a video. Both are now rows of
two-line cells, like the other long rows, and fit (skin_check.py, four
languages): of the labels that can scroll, three are left, all on pages behind
the overview and for values that only a diagnostic setting, a long RPU or a TV
tuner's name make that wide (eight in 1.0).

The two-line cells start 2 px higher, so that two lines of the small font hold
in the 64 px rows of the Dolby Vision page, which is 10 px higher for them; the
overview is 28 px higher where a row says how HDR10 is adapted, and its foot
moves up 86 px where none does (its columns hold in that, as checked). The
cells of the table of the levels take a width, a font and the place of their
dot, for a narrower table. The dialog of system/hades is made again.
